From: Marc Lainez <marc.lainez@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/nouveau/gm20b: Set voltage before initializing clock

gm20b_clk_init programs the lowest performance state directly, bypassing
the voltage request in nvkm_cstate_prog. On a Nano with the standard PWM
regulator range, the rail remains at its 710 mV minimum until the first
frequency transition, below the 818.75 mV minimum in the speedo-2 table.

Request the initial state's voltage before programming the PLL and its
noise-aware voltage detector. Only raise the voltage, preserving a higher
boot voltage until normal reclocking can lower it in the correct order.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-6
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/clk/gm20b.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/nouveau/nvkm/subdev/clk/gm20b.c
@@ -817,6 +817,14 @@ gm20b_clk_init(struct nvkm_clk *base)
 	int ret;
 	u32 data;
 
+	/* Establish the boot state's voltage before programming the PLL. */
+	ret = nvkm_volt_set_id(device->volt, base->func->pstates[0].base.voltage,
+			       base->func->pstates[0].base.voltage, base->temp, +1);
+	if (ret) {
+		nvkm_error(subdev, "cannot initialize voltage: %d\n", ret);
+		return ret;
+	}
+
 	/* get out from IDDQ */
 	nvkm_mask(device, GPCPLL_CFG, GPCPLL_CFG_IDDQ, 0);
 	nvkm_rd32(device, GPCPLL_CFG);
